<title>USA: Kimberly-Clark Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Kimberly-Clark Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $1.23     loss	 $3.01</p>
<p> Net profit	     347,100     loss     841,700</p>
<p> Net Sales	    3,323,600		3,297,900</p>
<p> Avg shrs		     N/A			N/A</p>
<p>12 MONTHS  Shr		 $4.98		    $0.12</p>
<p> Net		 1,403,800		33,200</p>
<p> Net Sales	 13,149,100	     13,373,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  N/A			N/A</p>
<p>	  (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Excluding non-operating items in both years, Q4 earnings from operations were a record $1.27/share vs $0.91.</p>
<p>Non-operating items included charges of $4.4 million, or $0.02 per share vs $81.1 million or $0.06 per share, for effects of translating dollar-denominated liabilities into Mexican pesos.</p>
<p>In 1996, the company's share of restructuring costs relating to the merger of Kimberly-Clark de Mexico with Scott Paper's former Mexican affiliate was $5.5 million, or $0.02 per share.</p>
</text>
